= November 2020 — Two kinds of street politics

Pandemic restrictions, the Women's Strike and the annual nationalist march
compete to define legitimate assembly.

[? if independence_march_strategy = "Civic tradition": Last year's small
Daszyński commemoration left organisers and a public identity to reuse. This
year decides whether it was an event or the beginning of an institution.?]
[? if independence_march_strategy = "Counter-mobilisation": Last year's
counter-mobilisation built trusted street contacts, but no separate account of
independence that can survive a public-health emergency.?]
[? if independence_march_strategy = "Legal monitoring": The observers return
with case files, lawyers and expectations. Abandoning them now would be a
decision, not an absence.?]

